My company's problem is that we have come from an OpenVMS platform. Our
infrastructure products, database, accounting systems, office automation etc. have
all over a number of years have been migrated and are available on Windows NT. While
AlphaNT existed we were having a very nice unhurried migration from Alpha OpenVMS to
Alpha NT.

We are still using the OpenVMS system and that's not a problem but our route to NT
must now be on Intel, AMD or Cytix.

We use project Primevera/SureTrack project planning software

CAD we use MicroStation and AutoCAD plus a number of add-ons.
 
For general use we use Office suite, Outlook, Exceed, Flash, Netscape, Explorer,
Dreamweaver, QuarkExpres, PC-Duo as well as a multitude of other minor applications.

We use Palm pilot and Psion integration software.

Are these available for Linux? (Don't bother anyone answering I know the answer).

I don't know the final count of AlphaNT native applications but although it wasn't
enough it wasn't insignificant either.

